"""Applied checks for critical misconceptions, with specific distractor diagnoses."""
from . import tutor,labs,refinements

CHECKS={
'lesson-03':('Real mode is selected but its credential is missing. What should startup do?',
 [('Reject startup with a field-only diagnostic.','Correct: fake mode is explicit, not an invisible fallback.'),('Switch to fake mode and return a plausible answer.','That hides a configuration failure behind fabricated success.'),('Print every environment value to find the problem.','That can disclose credentials unrelated to the error. Identify the missing field instead.')]),
'lesson-04':('One of three concurrent fixture calls times out. What protects the semaphore capacity?',
 [('Release the permit in finally and retain the failed result.','Failure must leave capacity available for later calls; gather with return_exceptions retains its outcome.'),('Decrement active only after successful calls.','The failing path would retain the active count and, in a manual semaphore implementation, could leak capacity.'),('Replace await with a blocking sleep.','That stalls the event loop and does not repair cleanup or failure reporting.')]),
'lesson-10':('Each retry needs 6 seconds including delay. The overall deadline is 15 seconds. How many fit?',
 [('Two attempts, totaling 12 seconds.','A third requires 18 seconds and must be refused before starting.'),('Three attempts because each timeout is below 15 seconds.','A per-attempt limit does not bound total elapsed time.'),('Retry authentication failures until the deadline.','An invalid credential is not a transient outage, regardless of remaining time.')]),
'lesson-13':('An answer cites a retrieved p1 but claims 90 days while p1 says 14. What do the checks establish?',
 [('Membership can pass; semantic support still fails separate review.','A known ID does not make the associated claim true.'),('The known citation proves the period is correct.','Membership only establishes source identity, not entailment of the text.'),('Every citation should be removed so the answer passes.','Removing evidence hides the contradiction; it does not make the answer supported.')]),
'lesson-15':('An accepted upload is marked ready without parsing or indexing. Which change preserves the lifecycle?',
 [('Reject the skipped transition and perform the intermediate work.','State records completed work, not a desired user-facing label.'),('Add accepted-to-ready to the allowed edges to satisfy the test.','That weakens the invariant and hides work that never happened.'),('Return ready in the API but retain accepted in storage.','The client would receive a false searchable status inconsistent with durable state.')]),
'lesson-18':('A request body names organization two, but the authenticated account belongs to one. What scope reaches retrieval?',
 [('Organization one, bound from authenticated identity.','Client-selected scope is untrusted and must not override the session.'),('Organization two because the request is more recent.','Recency does not grant authorization.'),('Both organizations, then remove private text from the final prose.','Unscoped retrieval can leak counts, metadata, traces and model context before final rendering.')]),
'lesson-25':('A worker writes a document row then fails before writing chunks. What must a transaction guarantee?',
 [('Neither partial write remains committed, so retry can perform the complete operation.','Atomicity covers the document and derived chunks together.'),('Keep the document ready because the ID was created.','An ID is not evidence of completed ingestion.'),('Use a retry key instead of a transaction.','The key prevents some duplicate effects but cannot roll back a partial multi-table write.')]),
'lesson-35':('Document and query vectors have equal dimensions but come from different embedding models. May they be mixed?',
 [('No; model/version identity must also match.','Equal width does not establish a common embedding space.'),('Yes, normalization makes every model space equivalent.','Normalization changes length, not the learned coordinate meaning.'),('Yes, if vector values are all positive.','Sign does not establish model compatibility or semantic geometry.')]),
'lesson-37':('Relevant passages are {b,c}; top two results are [a,b]. What is recall@2?',
 [('0.5, because one of the two relevant passages was retrieved.','The denominator is the distinct relevant set.'),('1.0, because the query had at least one relevant hit.','That describes a hit-rate success, not passage recall.'),('0.0, because the first result was irrelevant.','Recall@2 examines both results, not only the first rank.')]),
'lesson-38':('One ranking repeats a source ID twice. How should fusion treat it?',
 [('Count it once for that ranker, retaining a stable source ID.','Duplicates from one list must not create extra votes.'),('Add both contributions because repeated IDs imply confidence.','Repetition is not independent evidence and can inflate a source score.'),('Add lexical and vector raw scores directly instead.','Their raw scales differ; rank fusion avoids pretending they are calibrated.')]),
'lesson-41':('Refund policy v1 and delivery policy v2 are both retrieved. Is that alone a version conflict?',
 [('No; compare revisions within the same policy identity.','Different documents can legitimately have different version labels.'),('Yes; every passage in one context must share a version string.','That falsely conflates unrelated policy histories.'),('No conflict can ever occur when both passages have citations.','Citations preserve identity but do not resolve contradictory revisions of one policy.')]),
'lesson-47':('A judge always accepts and two of three independent human labels are unsupported. What must the report retain?',
 [('Two false acceptances, despite the judge appearing confident.','Independent labels expose a dangerous error category.'),('Perfect agreement because every output has a verdict.','Producing a verdict is not agreement with ground truth.'),('Relabel the human cases supported to match the judge.','That contaminates the reference labels and conceals calibration failure.')]),
'lesson-49':('The report omits scope isolation but every included check passes. May the gate release?',
 [('No; missing required evidence fails closed.','The required key set is independent of the submitted report.'),('Yes; all values present are True.','Checking only present values silently ignores a missing critical invariant.'),('Yes; replace the omitted check with a quality average.','A quality average cannot substitute for tenant isolation.')]),
'lesson-57':('Source and restored databases have equal counts. What additional evidence is necessary?',
 [('Read restored IDs, revisions and text from a fresh destination.','Equal counts can conceal wrong or corrupted content.'),('Copy the source Python dictionary and compare it to itself.','That exercises neither backup nor restoration.'),('Restore over the live source database to simplify comparison.','A disposable target permits verification without replacing the source being assessed.')]),
'lesson-59':('A load test excludes timed-out requests before reporting success rate. What is wrong?',
 [('Failures disappeared from the denominator, overstating useful service.','Retain every offered request and report errors alongside latency.'),('Nothing; failed requests have no user-visible cost.','Users waited for them and they may consume compute or provider usage.'),('Only successful latency matters when the average is low.','Fast successful calls cannot compensate for unreported failures or tail latency.')]),
'lesson-69':('Another user knows a checkpoint thread ID. What must the loader do before returning its state?',
 [('Check authenticated ownership and compatible schema version.','Thread identity locates state; it does not grant permission.'),('Return it because the ID was supplied correctly.','Knowing an identifier is not authorization.'),('Ask the model whether the user seems trustworthy.','An untrusted model judgment cannot replace authenticated ownership checks.')]),
'lesson-70':('A reviewer approved a draft event, then its destination changed. Is the old approval valid?',
 [('No; require approval for the exact changed payload and destination.','Approval binds the proposed effect, not the general idea of scheduling.'),('Yes, while the approval has not expired.','Expiry is only one gate; exact payload and actor binding must still match.'),('Yes, if the model says the change is harmless.','The model proposes content; it does not own the reviewer authorization.')]),
'lesson-71':('An operation key is replayed with different payload text. What should the ledger do?',
 [('Reject a conflicting replay rather than silently returning success.','Store payload identity with the scoped key and original result.'),('Execute again because the key is already known.','That permits a changed effect under a previously accepted identity.'),('Return the old receipt without comparing payloads.','That misrepresents which operation the receipt actually acknowledges.')]),
'lesson-77':('One required parallel search fails, while another returns evidence. How should the join report?',
 [('Retain the failure and block a complete-success claim.','Partial evidence can be useful but completeness is a separate contract.'),('Drop the failed branch and mark the remaining evidence complete.','That hides the required branch and inflates successful outcomes.'),('Retry every branch without a deadline until one answer looks good.','Unbounded retries amplify latency and cost while obscuring missing evidence.')]),
'lesson-84':('A tool response has isError=true but contains plausible policy prose. What may the client do?',
 [('Treat it as a tool failure, not evidence for an answer.','Check the envelope before consuming content.'),('Use the prose because it looks relevant.','Error content is not a successful retrieval result.'),('Set isError=false locally so downstream validation passes.','Changing the envelope conceals the server failure instead of handling it.')]),
'lesson-85':('A provider proposes finish while still supplying a non-null query. What happens?',
 [('The adapter rejects the action-specific schema violation before execution.','Finish requires query=null; the harness separately checks source membership.'),('The query is executed and then the finish is accepted.','A malformed proposal must not cause a side effect before validation.'),('The model automatically gains permission to change the harness.','The model proposes an action; application code retains authority.')]),
}
CHECKS.update({
 'terminal-01':('The terminal opens inside the academy application folder. What is the first student action?', [('Create and verify a separate scratch workspace before writing exercise files.','Relative paths resolve from the working directory, so inspect pwd first.'),('Create the exercise inside the app database folder.','That mixes course experiments with application state.'),('Assume the simulated mkdir command created a real directory.','The academy command box is stateless simulation and does not write your filesystem.')]),
 'terminal-02':('A process prints a plausible message but exits with code two. How should the caller classify it?', [('As failure, preserving stdout, stderr and the actual exit status.','The exit contract is explicit; text alone does not establish success.'),('As success because it printed something.','Programs can print before failing.'),('As success whenever stderr is empty.','A failing process need not write an error message; inspect its return code.')]),
 'terminal-03':('What should select([p1,p2,p3],0) return under the taught capacity policy?', [('An empty list, without modifying the original input.','Zero capacity admits no evidence; slicing returns a new list.'),('All three items because zero means unlimited.','That bypasses the explicit capacity boundary.'),('The original list with its last item removed.','That describes a negative slice bound, which this validator rejects as an invalid capacity.')]),
 'terminal-04':('A guarded module is imported rather than executed directly. What should happen?', [('Its functions become available without invoking the guarded CLI entry point.','The __name__ guard separates import from direct execution.'),('Its main block always starts because the file was read.','Import does not make __name__ equal __main__.'),('It must contact a provider before its pure function can be inspected.','The complete example has no network dependency.')]),
 'terminal-05':('The buggy validator accepts invented because the string is nonempty. Which repair matches the invariant?', [('Check membership in the retrieved source-ID set and retain the invented-source test.','Truthiness and evidence membership are different predicates.'),('Remove the invented-source test so the original function passes.','That hides the defect instead of repairing it.'),('Accept any longer citation string.','String length cannot establish source identity or support.')]),
 'terminal-06':('A local search function passed its tests. What protocol claim follows?', [('None; a real client/server transport test is a separate boundary.','Application tool behavior and MCP negotiation are distinct deliverables.'),('An MCP server has been deployed successfully.','No protocol connection or deployment occurred.'),('The function can now execute arbitrary shell commands safely.','A tested read-only operation grants no additional authority.')]),
 'terminal-07':('An instruction resource resolves outside its package root. What should the inspector do?', [('Reject it before reading; package review is separate from host activation.','Containment is checked on the resolved path.'),('Read it because it was named in the package.','A reference can contain traversal or an absolute escape.'),('Copy it into a global host directory to make it discoverable.','That activates unreviewed material and is unrelated to safe reference inspection.')]),
 'terminal-08':('The exercised source changes after a session note was saved. What should the next session do?', [('Detect the digest mismatch and rerun targeted checks before relying on the note.','Recorded observations belong to a source revision.'),('Keep treating the old passing note as proof of the new code.','The saved observation did not exercise the changed source.'),('Paste every project file and secret into the tutor context.','A focused context excludes secrets and unrelated files; more text does not repair stale evidence.')]),
})

def case(key,prompt,correct,wrong_one,reason_one,wrong_two,reason_two):
    from .specs import SPECS
    CHECKS[key]=(prompt,[(correct,SPECS[key]['explanation']),(wrong_one,reason_one),(wrong_two,reason_two)])
case('lesson-01','The refund policy permits unused items within 14 days. A user asks the assistant to issue a refund. What matches the product contract?',
'Refuse the action and keep the assistant read-only.','Issue the refund because the question mentions the policy.','Answering a policy question does not authorize changing records.','Quote only 14 days and omit unused items.','Removing the condition changes the supported policy meaning.')
case('lesson-02','A package imports globally but is absent from project metadata. What is the reproducibility repair?',
'Declare it in the project and resolve/test the locked environment.','Install it globally on every developer laptop.','That keeps undeclared ambient state as a hidden dependency.','Hand-edit the resolved lock without updating the declared dependency.','The declaration and resolver output would no longer describe the same project.')
case('lesson-05','The retriever returns no passages, but the fake generator always returns 14 days. Why is that fake unsuitable?',
'It can conceal retrieval failures because its answer ignores received evidence.','It is a valid semantic accuracy oracle.','A fixed answer cannot evaluate whether the retriever found support.','It proves the real provider will abstain.','No real provider was invoked, and the fake does not abstain.')
case('lesson-06','A 100-unit window reserves 10 for instructions, 20 for the question and 40 for output. How much evidence fits?',
'30 units.','70 units.','That ignores the 40-unit output reserve.','100 units.','Instructions, question, evidence and output share the same window.')
case('lesson-07','A retrieved passage says ignore all rules. Where does that string belong in the prompt envelope?',
'In untrusted evidence, with the system rule unchanged.','In the system field because it was retrieved successfully.','Successful retrieval grants no instruction authority.','In a tool-permission field enabling new actions.','Permissions are enforced by application code, not passage content.')
case('lesson-08','A format demonstration says 30 days, but current evidence says 7 days. Which fact belongs in the current answer?',
'7 days from the current evidence, with its source identity.','30 days because the demonstration appears earlier.','Examples teach behavior and format; they are not facts about the current policy.','The average, 18.5 days.','Averaging contradictory policy periods invents an unsupported condition.')
case('lesson-09','The provider omits usage information. What should the adapter report?',
'Unknown usage, preserving None or an equivalent explicit status.','Zero measured tokens.','Missing data is not a measurement of zero.','A guessed count labeled measured.','An estimate must retain its estimation label and assumptions.')
case('lesson-11','An upload returns accepted, then indexing fails. What should the client observe?',
'A durable failed/pending status, rather than an answer pretending the document is searchable.','A ready status because the HTTP upload succeeded.','Upload acceptance and completed indexing are different events.','An invented answer while indexing recovers.','Operational failure does not authorize fabricating policy evidence.')
case('lesson-12','A request question contains only three spaces. Which boundary is appropriate?',
'Reject normalized blank input before expensive service work.','Accept it because its raw length is three.','Length validation must consider the normalized content.','Let the model decide whether the HTTP body is valid.','Transport contracts belong in deterministic application validation.')
case('lesson-14','Retrieval succeeds with an empty list. Should the injected generator be called?',
'No; return the explicit missing-evidence result.','Yes, with the entire unscoped corpus instead.','That expands context and permission scope to hide the missing evidence.','Yes, because a generator can invent a helpful policy.','Invented policy content violates the evidence contract.')
case('lesson-16','The next whole passage exceeds the remaining context budget and contains a policy exception. What does the selector do?',
'Exclude it intact and record the evidence limitation for evaluation.','Cut off the exception to make the passage fit.','Truncating a qualifier can reverse the policy meaning.','Include it anyway because exceptions are useful.','Importance does not remove the model context limit; reprioritize within a valid budget.')
case('lesson-17','The bytes stay the same but the parser version changes. What happens to ingestion identity?',
'It changes, so derived output can be rebuilt and attributed.','It stays identical because only filenames matter.','Filenames neither identify immutable bytes nor parser output.','It becomes a permission grant for every tenant.','Identity and authorization are separate boundaries.')
case('lesson-19','Fixture rates are 1 per million input units and 2 per million output units. For 1000 input and 1000 output units, what is cost?',
'0.003 fixture currency units.','0.002 because all tokens use the input rate.','Output has its own rate and must be counted separately.','3 because per-million rates apply per thousand.','The denominator is one million units, not one thousand.')
case('lesson-20','The chosen architecture is a read-only pipeline. Which change justifies revisiting that decision?',
'A new requirement for approved write operations.','A new UI theme.','A theme does not change the execution authority or task workflow.','A preference for adding more agents to the diagram.','Complexity needs a task benefit supported by evidence, not visual appeal.')
case('lesson-21','GET /health succeeds, but GET /missing has no route. Which outcome is appropriate?',
'404 with a bounded not-found response.','200 with the health body for every path.','That hides missing routes and makes client integration errors look successful.','A fabricated document answer.','An HTTP routing failure is unrelated to generation or source evidence.')
case('lesson-22','The provider times out. How should the route differ from a successful search with no evidence?',
'Return a classified retryable service error; missing evidence remains a successful abstention.','Return the same empty successful answer in both cases.','That hides an operational outage and contaminates evaluation counts.','Expose the upstream exception including credentials.','Public diagnostics should use stable codes without sensitive values.')
case('lesson-23','Two concurrent ingestions use the same tenant and content digest. Which mechanism arbitrates duplicates?',
'The database UNIQUE constraint on scoped identity.','A Python precheck alone.','Both workers can pass a precheck before either commits.','A globally unique filename chosen by the user.','A filename does not establish content identity or race-safe uniqueness.')
case('lesson-24','An additive migration adds a state column to existing document rows. Which default preserves honest status?',
'Accepted, followed by actual ingestion before ready.','Ready, because the row already existed.','Existing metadata is not evidence that the new ingestion workflow completed.','Delete existing rows to avoid assigning a default.','That destroys data instead of demonstrating a compatible additive change.')
case('lesson-26','A worker receives an already-ready document again. What should happen?',
'Return the completed state without duplicating its chunks.','Create another set of chunks because delivery occurred twice.','At-least-once delivery needs idempotent application effects.','Set it ready without ever processing its first delivery.','A job ID or delivery event is not evidence of transformed data.')
case('lesson-27','A file format is unsupported and the queue is saturated. Should the worker retry it automatically?',
'No; it is a permanent input failure and queue pressure also blocks admission.','Yes, because all exceptions are transient.','Unsupported bytes do not become supported through repeated attempts.','Yes, without a bound because capacity will eventually return.','Unbounded retries amplify load and do not repair the invalid input.')
case('lesson-28','The Dockerfile says EXPOSE 8010. Can a host browser reach it automatically?',
'No; the host port still needs an explicit publication.','Yes; EXPOSE publishes it on every host interface.','EXPOSE documents a container port; it does not configure host binding.','Only if the process runs as root.','A process user does not replace network publication or binding configuration.')
case('lesson-29','The API process is alive but its required database probe fails. What should readiness return?',
'Unavailable until the dependency recovers.','Ready because the process has a PID.','Process existence does not establish usable dependencies.','A successful model answer cached from another tenant.','A cache cannot bypass ownership or a required readiness contract.')
case('lesson-30','A model supplies True as the search limit. What should the plain Python validator do?',
'Reject it because the contract requires an exact integer type.','Treat it as a valid integer limit of one.','Python bool subclasses int, but that language relation does not satisfy this explicit input contract.','Use it to enable write access.','The limit field has no authority to change tool capabilities.')
case('lesson-31','A UTF-8 parser reads a blank file. What should ingestion record?',
'An explicit extraction failure, not a searchable empty document.','A ready document with invented fallback text.','No extractable text exists to support the invented content.','A claim that OCR succeeded.','Reading UTF-8 does not exercise OCR or PDF extraction.')
case('lesson-32','With size 4 and overlap 0, how is abcdefgh split?',
'Into abcd and efgh.','Into abcd, defg and gh.','Those starts use overlap one and stride three.','Into infinitely many windows at the same offset.','A valid positive size with zero overlap has stride four; overlap equal to size must be rejected.')
case('lesson-33','Policy v1 position zero and policy v2 position zero contain different text. Which chunk identity policy is correct?',
'Keep distinct immutable revision-based IDs.','Reuse an ID that always resolves to the latest text.','Old citations would appear to cite evidence the answer never saw.','Use only position zero as the identity.','Position is not globally unique across documents, revisions or tenants.')
case('lesson-34','Two lexical results tie on score. How should the baseline order them?',
'Use a stable source-ID tie-breaker.','Use whichever row the database happens to return first.','Unspecified order can change evaluations without a meaningful implementation change.','Return a zero-score unrelated row first.','Zero-score candidates should not displace matching evidence in this baseline.')
case('lesson-36','The closest vector belongs to another tenant. What is the correct ranking boundary?',
'Filter tenant scope before distance ranking.','Retrieve the global nearest row, then hide its text in the UI.','Counts, traces and model context may already leak before the final UI filter.','Allow it because vector similarity is high.','Similarity is not authorization.')
case('lesson-39','The needed passage is outside the candidate limit. Can the reranker recover it?',
'No; improve candidate retrieval or widen its evaluated budget.','Yes; reranking invents missing candidates.','A reranker can only rescore the candidate set it receives.','Yes; discard all source IDs and ask for a new answer.','Discarding provenance hides the retrieval problem instead of correcting it.')
case('lesson-40','The database contains p1, but the context sent to generation contains only p2. May the answer cite p1?',
'No; citation membership must use the evidence actually sent.','Yes; any database row is an allowed citation.','Database presence does not establish that the generator received or used that source.','Yes, if the answer sounds fluent.','Tone does not establish evidence membership or factual support.')
case('lesson-42','An untrusted passage asks the agent to delete documents. Which enforcement is essential?',
'The harness denies tools outside its read-only allowlist.','A keyword filter alone guarantees safety.','An attacker can paraphrase; authority must remain enforced outside the model.','Move the passage into the system instruction.','That promotes untrusted content into an authority channel.')
case('lesson-43','An evaluation labels a query answerable but lists no relevant source IDs. What should the dataset builder do?',
'Review and repair the inconsistent label before using the case.','Assume the system is wrong regardless of source availability.','A labeling defect can be mistaken for a model or retrieval failure.','Copy the candidate model answer into the expected label.','That contaminates independent evaluation with the system under test.')
case('lesson-44','An answer states the wrong period but cites a known source. Which metric catches the unsupported fact?',
'A separate semantic support assessment against the source.','Citation membership alone.','The ID can be real while its associated claim is false.','Checking that text is a string.','A valid type says nothing about whether the claim follows from evidence.')
case('lesson-45','Two worker stages belong to the same request. What makes their trace useful without exposing raw text?',
'A shared request ID, stage names and measured durations with allowlisted metadata.','Logging every private passage and credential.','Sensitive payload is unnecessary for stage correlation and creates exposure.','Giving each stage an unrelated random ID with no parent link.','That loses the causal relationship needed to diagnose one request.')
case('lesson-46','The provider reports zero tokens on one request and omits usage on another. How should the report represent them?',
'Distinguish measured zero from unknown usage.','Record both as zero.','That understates spending and erases measurement availability.','Replace both with a precise invented estimate.','Estimated usage must not be labeled as a measured observation.')
case('lesson-48','A prompt experiment also changes chunk size. What conclusion is justified by a quality difference?',
'The combined change differs; the prompt-specific cause is not isolated.','The prompt alone caused the difference.','Two changed variables prevent that attribution.','The result is reproducible without recording either version.','Configuration identity is necessary to reproduce the compared inputs.')
case('lesson-50','A test verifies TimeoutGenerator.generate exists but never calls it through the service. What is missing?',
'Actual failure injection and assertions on the public error outcome.','A more descriptive method name.','Naming does not execute the failing dependency or test classification.','A passing answer substituted for the timeout.','That removes the failure path the test needs to exercise.')
case('lesson-51','A target supports HTTP routes but not long-running workers or durable storage. Does it meet this stack requirement?',
'No; the worker and persistence requirements need supported services.','Yes, because any HTTP server can run arbitrary background jobs durably.','A request runtime does not imply a durable worker lifecycle.','Yes, if the target is cheaper.','Lower cost does not satisfy missing runtime capabilities.')
case('lesson-52','Staging has a database configured but debug is enabled. What should startup do?',
'Reject the unsafe configuration before serving requests.','Start and print the full database URL for review.','The URL may contain credentials, and printing it does not disable debug.','Assume a successful image build makes runtime settings safe.','Build success and runtime configuration validation are separate gates.')
case('lesson-53','A direct public client sends X-Forwarded-Proto: https over plain HTTP. What does the app trust?',
'Its actual transport, unless the forwarding peer is explicitly trusted.','The header from any client.','Clients can forge forwarded headers.','A generated answer saying the connection is secure.','Connection security is a transport configuration fact, not model output.')
case('lesson-54','The evaluation subprocess exits one after unit tests pass. What should CI do next?',
'Stop before building or promoting the candidate.','Build and release because the unit tests passed.','The required evaluation gate failed independently.','Change the shell command to always exit zero.','That hides the failing evidence instead of enforcing the release contract.')
case('lesson-55','The candidate image fails health after a destructive schema change. Is switching the image tag a sufficient recovery plan?',
'No; compatibility and data recovery need explicit review.','Yes; the previous image restores deleted data automatically.','An image rollback does not reverse destructive data changes.','Yes; health is irrelevant once deployment began.','Failed readiness is evidence against promoting the candidate.')
case('lesson-56','A new event field unexpectedly contains private document text. Which scrubbing strategy excludes it by default?',
'An allowlist of permitted diagnostic fields.','Removing only a field named api_key.','Sensitive content can appear under many names.','Printing it once to confirm the scrubber saw it.','That is already an exposure; verify with synthetic values instead.')
case('lesson-58','An upload is deleted but its answer cache remains. What must deletion also address?',
'Derived chunks and revision/owner-scoped cached answers.','Only the visible upload filename.','Derived stores can retain the content after the original disappears.','Every other tenant’s unrelated documents.','Deletion must respect scope and preserve unrelated data.')
case('lesson-60','A release report has passing tests and evaluation but recovery is unknown. What is the honest decision?',
'Blocked pending recovery evidence, not a production-ready claim.','Approved because unknown is not explicitly false.','Missing required evidence fails closed.','Rename unknown to observed_pass without a drill.','Changing a report string does not create an observation.')
case('lesson-61','The step budget ends immediately after a search. What may the harness report?',
'An explicit step_budget stop without a completed answer.','A completed answer because evidence was found.','A tool result is not a validated final response.','A larger invisible budget so the run looks successful.','Silently extending the budget removes the termination guarantee being tested.')
case('lesson-62','A proposal requests delete instead of the allowed search operation. When should it be rejected?',
'Before tool execution or any side effect.','After running it so the result can be inspected.','Validation after a destructive side effect is too late.','Only if the model expresses low confidence.','Confidence is not execution authority.')
case('lesson-63','A plan starts with valid search but later requests a denied shell operation. How should prevalidation behave?',
'Reject the whole invalid plan before executing the earlier step.','Execute all steps and label the plan invalid afterward.','The plan would already have performed unreviewed effects.','Treat the word plan as approval for every operation.','Planning and authorization are separate boundaries.')
case('lesson-64','A source revision changes while the tenant and question stay the same. What should happen to the context cache key?',
'It must change or invalidate so stale evidence is not reused.','It stays the same because the question is identical.','The answer depends on source revision as well as question.','Remove tenant scope to improve cache hit rate.','Cross-tenant reuse can disclose private evidence.')
case('lesson-65','Both allowed repair attempts produce unsupported drafts. Which terminal verdict is correct?',
'Rejected, with attempts exhausted recorded separately.','Accepted because the loop ended normally.','Termination and acceptance are different facts.','Retry forever until the verifier agrees.','That removes the cost and latency bound.')
case('lesson-66','A trace contains finish but the final status is unsupported_citation. What should diagnosis inspect?',
'The proposed source ID against the actual observations.','Only whether finish appears in the trace.','A finish proposal can be rejected by validation.','The UI color used to display the answer.','Display styling does not explain a source-membership failure.')
case('lesson-67','The task always follows retrieve, draft, verify. Which baseline should precede dynamic planning?',
'An explicit fixed workflow evaluated on the same cases.','An unconstrained agent with every available tool.','Additional autonomy needs evidence of task benefit and bounded authority.','A diagram with no executable failure checks.','A diagram does not establish behavior or provide a regression baseline.')
case('lesson-68','A rejected graph state has already used both repair attempts. Where should routing go?',
'A failed terminal state rather than an accepted finish.','Repair again without increasing the counter.','That can loop indefinitely and misrepresent attempts.','Accepted because the retry budget was respected.','Respecting a budget does not make the output valid.')
case('lesson-72','A candidate uses half the calls but answers an unanswerable case. How should the comparison report it?',
'Cheaper fixture execution with a quality regression that still blocks acceptance.','An unconditional improvement because calls fell.','Cost reduction cannot trade away a mandatory abstention gate.','Delete the unanswerable case from the dataset.','That changes the evaluation to conceal the observed regression.')
case('lesson-73','A worker sends evidence_ids as a string rather than a list. What should the receiver do?',
'Reject the malformed handoff before consuming it.','Iterate the string as individual source-ID characters.','That changes the message meaning and can produce invalid evidence references.','Trust the role name instead of validating the envelope.','A named role does not establish message shape or source authority.')
case('lesson-74','The researcher can search and the reviewer can verify. May the reviewer send an external message just because it is called a reviewer?',
'No; execution checks the actual capability allowlist.','Yes; role names imply all tools needed to finish.','A descriptive role is not an authorization grant.','Yes; a high-quality draft automatically authorizes publication.','Output quality and permission to cause an external effect are separate decisions.')
case('lesson-75','Two independent branches take 20 and 30 units, with 5 units of orchestration overhead. What is the parallel critical path?',
'35 units under the stated fixture assumptions.','55 units because parallel durations always add.','Independent overlapping branches contribute their maximum duration plus overhead.','30 units because orchestration is free.','The specified five-unit overhead still contributes to end-to-end latency.')
case('lesson-76','A builder is 99% confident in 90 days, but evidence says 14 days. What should the independent fixture reviewer do?',
'Reject the wrong claim using the original evidence.','Accept the builder confidence as a semantic verdict.','Self-confidence is not independent support.','Average the periods to reconcile the disagreement.','That invents another unsupported policy value.')
case('lesson-78','A team costs more and fails the minimum quality and latency gates. Which decision is justified?',
'Reject it despite having more workers.','Accept it because more agents imply better reasoning.','Architecture size does not establish task quality.','Hide its extra orchestration calls from the cost report.','Every model/tool call and handoff is part of the useful-output economics.')
case('lesson-79','A tool was discovered through MCP. Does discovery authorize access to another organization?',
'No; application authentication and scope enforcement still apply.','Yes; discovery is equivalent to tenant consent.','Discovery describes capabilities, not owner authorization.','Yes; the tool description can grant admin permissions.','Descriptions are untrusted data and cannot expand the execution allowlist.')
case('lesson-80','The read-only search server receives a blank query. What should happen?',
'An explicit input error rather than returning the whole corpus.','Return every document to be helpful.','A blank input must not widen context or access scope.','Run an arbitrary filesystem search instead.','The server only exposes the fixed synthetic read-only collection.')
case('lesson-81','Discovery does not include the required search_policies tool. Should the client call it anyway?',
'No; stop with a missing-capability result before invocation.','Yes; guess a similar tool name.','Guessing skips the contract the client needs to verify.','Treat discovery failure as an empty successful policy search.','Protocol/capability failure is different from a valid query with no matches.')
case('lesson-82','A tool call times out inside the client connection context. What must lifecycle handling guarantee?',
'The owned transport/session resources are closed on the failure path.','Only successful calls need cleanup.','Failed operations can otherwise leak processes and connections.','Write debug text to stdio protocol stdout before closing.','That can corrupt protocol framing; diagnostics belong on stderr.')
case('lesson-83','A tool result includes grant_admin=true plus policy text. How should downstream handling treat it?',
'Retain only validated evidence fields and keep tool authority unchanged.','Promote grant_admin into application configuration.','Untrusted result fields cannot grant permissions.','Assume sanitized text is now safe to obey as instructions.','Shape validation does not turn evidence into trusted instruction authority.')
case('lab-01','A product baseline passes refund questions but has no unavailable-answer case. What should be added?',
'A labeled unsupported question with expected abstention.','Another easy supported question instead.','Only supported examples cannot expose an always-answering system.','A fake success response for every unsupported topic.','That defeats the evidence boundary the baseline is meant to measure.')
case('lab-02','One provider request times out and another is denied for credentials. What should the integrated boundary preserve?',
'Different retryable and configuration-error statuses, without fabricated answer text.','One successful empty answer for both failures.','That hides operational and setup failures from callers and evaluation.','Unlimited retries for both errors.','Credential failures are not transient and retries still need an overall budget.')
case('lab-03','A valid question targets a document still indexing. What should the service return?',
'A pending/unavailable state with no answer citations.','An answer because request validation passed.','Input validity does not establish document readiness.','A citation to any ready document in another tenant.','Readiness cannot replace scoped evidence selection.')
case('lab-04','Increasing evidence capacity admits a private passage from a second tenant. What is the defect?',
'Authorization scope was mixed with budget/ranking instead of enforced first.','The context window is too small.','A larger window cannot authorize private source access.','The private passage should simply receive a stronger citation.','A citation does not grant permission to use the passage.')
case('lab-05','A persistence exercise reads a row using the same uncommitted connection that wrote it. What evidence is still missing?',
'Commit, close and reopen through a new connection before readback.','A different variable name for the same connection.','Renaming does not test durable visibility.','A copied Python object containing the expected value.','That does not read the persisted database at all.')
case('lab-06','The queue returns a task ID but the worker never transforms the document. What is the correct status claim?',
'Accepted work, with completion still unverified.','Completed ingestion because a task was queued.','A job identifier proves dispatch at most, not transformed durable data.','Ready after manually editing a status string.','That bypasses the worker and can expose incomplete searchable state.')
case('lab-07','A revised policy is chunked at the same positions as its previous version. What must remain distinct?',
'The revision-based chunk identities used for citations.','Only the display title.','A title does not preserve immutable evidence identity.','Nothing; old answers should silently cite the new text.','That would change what past answers appear to have used as evidence.')
case('lab-08','Both relevant vector fixtures are retrieved at k=2, but only one at k=1. What should the report show?',
'Recall falls from 1.0 to 0.5 with relevance labels unchanged.','Recall stays 1.0 because there was still one hit.','One successful query hit does not mean every relevant passage was retrieved.','The labels should shrink to whichever result was returned.','Candidate output must not redefine independent relevance ground truth.')
case('lab-09','A hybrid retriever improves the mean but regresses a policy-exception query. What should be retained?',
'The per-query regression and its release significance.','Only the improved average.','An average can conceal a critical missing condition.','A report with the regressed query removed.','Removing the failing case hides evidence rather than repairing retrieval.')
case('lab-10','One case cites an invented ID; another cites a real ID with the wrong fact. How should the report classify them?',
'Separate citation-structure and semantic-support failures.','Both pass whenever the output is valid JSON.','Serialization shape does not establish source identity or factual support.','Treat a known ID as enough to accept the wrong fact.','A real source can be cited while its content is misrepresented.')
case('lab-11','The trace totals retrieval, generation and validation but excludes a retry delay. What should change?',
'Include the retry in end-to-end duration and usage accounting where available.','Leave it out because the final attempt succeeded.','Users still experienced the delay and retries can consume resources.','Record missing token usage as a measured zero.','Unknown usage must stay distinguishable from an observed zero.')
case('lab-12','An intentionally broken critical check still makes the gate executable exit zero. What failed?',
'The gate itself failed to propagate rejection to CI.','The failure injection was unnecessary.','Testing the reject path is how the gate contract is verified.','The candidate must be good because the pipeline is green.','A green pipeline can be caused by swallowed failure exits.')
case('lab-13','The candidate responds to health, but its schema is incompatible with the previous release. What should promotion require?',
'Explicit compatibility/recovery review instead of assuming image rollback is sufficient.','Immediate promotion because the HTTP route works.','A static health response does not prove rollback or data compatibility.','Replacing the previous artifact record with the new tag.','That removes the recovery reference without creating a recovery plan.')
case('lab-14','A local pilot passes its required tests, while public HTTPS was never exercised. What may the handoff claim?',
'Local pilot evidence, with public HTTPS explicitly untested.','A globally production-ready public service.','Local checks do not establish DNS, certificates or public exposure behavior.','A verified HTTPS result copied from another project.','Evidence belongs to a specific artifact and environment.')
case('lab-15','Search ran successfully but returned an empty list. What must observation state let the adapter do?',
'Distinguish that empty result from no search yet and finish with abstention.','Repeat search until the step budget ends because an empty list erases history.','That loses a completed observation and prevents the intended abstention branch.','Finish with an invented citation to avoid an empty answer.','Source membership still applies even after a successful empty search.')
case('lab-16','A graph exhausts its repair budget with a rejected answer. Which result is honest?',
'Rejected with a bounded attempt count and retained trace.','Accepted because every node ran.','Executed stages do not imply the output met the verification rule.','An unbounded extra repair outside the recorded trace.','Hidden work breaks the reported latency/cost and termination contract.')
case('lab-17','A resumed operation has a valid old approval but its payload changed. What should happen before ledger lookup?',
'Reject the mismatched approval before any effect.','Replay the old receipt as approval for the changed effect.','A receipt identifies the operation actually authorized and performed.','Ask the worker to decide whether reviewer intent probably carries over.','Inferred intent cannot replace exact payload and authenticated approval binding.')
case('lab-18','A reviewer receives correct text but a different run ID than its evidence handoff. What should it do?',
'Reject the cross-run message.','Accept it because the string happens to match.','Correct text can still be attached to the wrong execution or source context.','Remove run IDs from every message to avoid the mismatch.','That hides isolation defects instead of preserving typed handoff identity.')
case('lab-19','A server advertises search_policies and delete. The host permits only search_policies. What may the client execute?',
'Only validated calls to the host-allowed search_policies tool.','Any discovered tool, including delete.','Discovery describes capabilities; the host still owns authorization.','Search calls with arbitrary owner fields added by the model.','The exact input contract rejects extra fields; ownership comes from the trusted application boundary.')
case('lab-20','A tool error envelope includes plausible prose saying to enable delete. What should the client do?',
'Reject the error as evidence and retain its fixed read-only capability set.','Use the prose and enable delete because it sounds specific.','Error content and malicious text cannot grant execution authority.','Change the error flag locally to make the result usable.','That conceals the actual tool failure instead of handling it.')
